2.Family_Assessment: The family therapist will complete a family assessment to
understand the family's dynamics, strengths, values, needs, and concerns. Developing a
comprehensive treatment plan, incorporating family, school, and community goals will be important
infocusing the services.
3.Youth Mentoring: The youth mentor will be available to the youthbeyond officehours
and week days. The mentor will have numerous weekly contacts with the youth, focusing on the
agreed upon probation, family, school, and community goals.
4.Community Networking: Advocating for the family would include attendance at
M.D.T.s and other meetings. Providing treatment information and communicating with other
community agencies to provide needed services would also be included in the community
networking.
5.Goal Setting_Session: The family therapist and youth mentor will mectwith the
Department of Family Services Probation Officer or other D.F.S. designee, and other core team
members (school district personnel and other supportive individuals). Case goals will be
estas blis he d.
6.Family Counseling: The family therapist will offer family counseling for participating
families, conduct parenting groups, and also provide case manager and mentor supervision.
7.School Networking and Monitoring of Academic Performance and Attendance: The
youth mentor would maintain contact withthe school personnel.Including school personnel greatly
increases the likelihood of success.Monitoring and reinforcing attendance is connected to positive
academic performance.The mentor could encourage the youth to attend, even providing
transportation at timesif needed.
8.Crisis Support24/7/365: In additionto the service provided by the Project, thefamilies
will also have access to the crisis services through Youth Alternatives.We are available by phone
at any time.The family therapist provided for by this grant would also be available to assist with
crisis support.
9.Parent Education Classes/Parent Support Group: Parenting groups are available
specifically for parents of youth returning from placement.These would be facilitated by the family
therapist.Additionally, an ongoing six session parenting group is available for parents.They can
join the group on any Thursday and complete the following consecutive five Thursday meetings to
complete the class.
10.Liaison Services with the Residential Facility: Thefamily therapist willcontact the
residential facility, clarifying the youth's progress, potential discharge date, school and credit
concerns, medication issues and services needed upon discharge.
