J.Program Operating Hours
The program will be essentially 24/7 for the entire year of the funding.The mentor is
typically on call 24/7 to respond to any concerns, questions, calls or texts from the youth. She does
a significant amount of work on the weekends and after regular business hours.The family
counseloris often available 24/7as well.Family sessions are coordinated and scheduled at times
when thefamilyis available, with most of the sessions facilitated in the home.At times when the
counselor is not available, the on-call emergency service operated through Youth Alternatives is
always available. These families are granted significant and easy access to our services.
K.Performance Measures
1.Percentage of youth successfully transitioning into theirhome, avoiding anotherout-
of home residential placement.
2.Percentage of youth who are placed in a lesser restrictive setting - like foster care.
3.Percentage of students successfully returning and staying in their home school.
4.Percentage of students remaining enrolled in school will be determined.
5.Percent of youth who are positively released from probation.
6.Monthly evaluations will be obtained from the parents and youth tomake sure we are
providing needed and appropriate services.
7.Termination evaluations will be obtained from families participating in the program.
