L.Data Collection Methods
Thefamily therapist will be responsible for obtaining the following data from families
referred to Project H.O.M.E.:
1.Number of families accepted into the program
2.Monthly evaluation forms will be filled out by family members to receive feedback
regarding their satisfaction with the services they'vereceived.
3.Percentage ofyouth remaining in school will be obtained at the 180 day time frame.
4.Percentage of youth remaining in their home will be obtained at the180 day time
frame.
The case manager willkeep track of number of referrals, dates of referrals, termination dates,
number of placements, number of second placements, and other outcomes like being positively
released from probation, new charges the r program or la cements like ob Corps or the at ional
Guard Boot Camp.This information will be tracked and presented as youth leave the program and
as the year of their discharge occurs.
M. Program Replication
Replication ofthe program in other areas canbe done relatively easily ifthere are trained
marriage and family therapists available.The assessment format and forms generated to track the
families and youth would be shared.Wewould be glad to consult with other counties to assist in
the implementation of a similar program.
N. Program Evaluation
EVALUATION TOOLS TO MEASURE PROGRAM OUTCOME
1.Percentage of youth remaining in their home, avoiding another out-of home
placement.
2.Percentage of students successfully returning and staying in their home school.
3.Percentage of students remaining enrolled in school will be determined.
4.Monthly evaluations will be obtained from the parents and youth to make sure we are
providing needed and appropriate services.
5.Termination evaluations will be obtained from families participating in the program.
O.Track Results One Year Post Program
The family counselor will keep track ofthe number of referrals made to the program.At
one year anniversaries of termination, the case managerwill contact either the Department of Family
Services or the District Attorney's Office to determine ifa second out-of-home placement occurred.
Other important data will be school/academic progres, succss on probation, job retention, and
positive movement into self-sufficiency.
