COST-BENEFITS:
The grant award of $22,400would provide transitional services foryouth, the family, an
the core team.Thefunding would continue the work with the presently referred youth and their
families and for up to twenty newfamily referrals.The cost of out-of-home placements is
approximately $48,000 -$60,000/year.If Project H.O.M.E.keeps youth in their homes, avoiding
another out of home placement, the savings would be significant.Keeping even one child from
returning to a placement would more than double the cost of this program in savings.
Additionally, iftheyouth ends up in another placement and not withhis family, that
initial placement investment has notbeen cost effective, nor didit reach the intended goal.Plus
additional funds need to be expended for the second placement.
This of course only deals with the financial cost, and does not begin to address the
emotional concerns or the life-long pattern of behavior that becomes ingrained in a young person,
often resulting in involvement with the adult legal systemfor many years.
Keeping twoyouth out of placement would payfor the program.
Other Funding Sources
We believe that we are all in this together and the kids in Cheyenne are all of our kids.
Because of that we are applying to get this grant to help cover the costs of actually providinga
program that would benefit ourkids, ourfamilies and our community.However, clearly the
phone costs, mileage, and other supportive services costs will continue tobe supported
supplemented by our general budget.
